A||N||5||GML||Need help setting the timing on 85 GT||||5||
Z||000000||GML||04-03-2000||05:45 PM||||I have recently rebuilt the engine on my 85 GT, but I am having a problem getting the timing set.  I've followed the manuals instructions but have had no luck.  I need help!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||04-03-2000||05:49 PM||||You did put the computer in dianostic mode first right?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GML||04-03-2000||06:14 PM||||Yes, my biggest problem is finding the timing mark on the damper. <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>You did put the computer in dianostic mode first right?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Cooter||04-03-2000||06:21 PM||||Do you have the distributer indexed properly to the number 1 cylinder? How did you install the distributer in relation to the cam/crank timing marks? It is possible that you have the distributer 1/2 of a round out of time.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GML||04-03-2000||06:43 PM||||I think I have it indexed properly, but am not sure because I am unsure which mark to set the timing by on the damper. <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>Do you have the distributer indexed properly to the number 1 cylinder? How did you install the distributer in relation to the cam/crank timing marks? It is possible that you have the distributer 1/2 of a round out of time.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||daved||04-03-2000||09:00 PM||||When I got my 86GT, drove it for some time and figured it lacked some power.  While changing plugs, thought to check the timing (with diagnostic mode on!) only to find I couldn't see the mark. On peering around for a bit, I could just catch a glimpse of the mark towards 12 o'clock...I would guess at least 12 deg. after TDC.  Retimed it and things are dramatically better (need I say?)<BR>Also noted that the previous owner had the distributor 180 deg. from where the Haynes shows it. Just prove its position by checking #1 on compression stroke, and ensure that pointy thing on the rotor/ dist. cap goes to #1 cylinder, hope this helps D.||||reg||1
